uring fertilization, and also plays a role in the regulation of proteins involved in spermatogenesis (By similarity). Regulates protein pathways that promote chromosomal synapsis formation, double-strand break repair, formation of the inner mitochondrial membrane cristae and apoptosis in developing sperm (By similarity). Required for normal sperm motility and binding to the zona pellucida, potentially via a role in ADAM3 protein maturation (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}